From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: an absolute mouse is a mouse

evdev read QEMU's USB tablet as a touchscreen. It has absolute X and Y,
five mouse buttons and a wheel, and no `BTN_TOUCH`, and
`ProbeLegacyAbsoluteDevice` calls any such device with `BTN_LEFT` a
touchscreen. A click was a tap, the wheel and the right and middle
buttons were dropped, and nothing hovered.

- `EventDeviceInfo::HasAbsoluteMouse`: the legacy probe's `BTN_LEFT`
  branch is a mouse when there is also a `BTN_RIGHT`. A touchscreen that
  clicks with `BTN_LEFT` alone (the Elo 2700) stays a touchscreen; pens,
  `BTN_TOUCH` touchscreens and the denylisted ILITEK are untouched.
- `CreateConverter` gives it `AbsoluteMouseEventConverterEvdev`
  (`ui/events/ozone/evdev/domicile/`): position moves the pointer, every
  mouse button and both wheels (high-resolution where the device has
  it) are a mouse's.
- `CursorDelegateEvdev::GetDomicileAbsoluteArea`: where a device's range
  goes. `DrmCursor` answers the display `input.pointers` binds it to
  (`SetDomicileAbsoluteAreas`, fed by `DrmPointerTargets`), otherwise
  the confined bounds, as the pen tablet uses. The default is out of
  line in the new `cursor_delegate_evdev.cc`, as the style plugin wants.
- `DrmCursor::MoveCursorTo` from the evdev thread moves onto the window
  under the location, so a device bound to another display reaches it.
- `ozone_unittests` builds the converter's test, which reads devices
  from captured capabilities; evdev's `event_device_info` targets let it.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
